<section class="section-shell orientation-section" aria-labelledby="signals-heading">
  <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Signals from the world</p>
    <h2 id="signals-heading">Your concern has context.</h2>
    <p>These signals do not tell one simple story. They show why orientation now requires more than following one headline, institution, platform, or field.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="orientation-grid">
    <article class="orientation-card">
      <p class="pathway-number" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
      <p class="orientation-label">Population survey · June 2026</p>
      <h3>Work and livelihood</h3>
      <p>71% of U.S. adults think AI will lead to fewer jobs over the next 20 years. That is a public expectation—not proof of the eventual labor-market outcome.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/18/young-adults-in-the-us-are-increasingly-wary-of-ai-concerned-it-will-take-jobs/">Review the Pew evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>

    <article class="orientation-card">
      <p class="pathway-number" aria-hidden="true">02</p>
      <p class="orientation-label">Population survey · April 2026</p>
      <h3>Climate and security</h3>
      <p>65% of Americans say global warming is personally important to them. Climate concern sits alongside economic, technological, political, and family concerns—not outside them.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://climatecommunication.yale.edu/app/uploads/2026/07/climate-change-american-mind-beliefs-attitudes-spring-2026.pdf">Review the Yale–GMU report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>

    <article class="orientation-card">
      <p class="pathway-number" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
      <p class="orientation-label">Expert assessment · July 2026</p>
      <h3>Information and reality</h3>
      <p>In one study of 54 international experts, video deepfakes received the highest average threat rating among AI-disinformation formats. The finding maps expert perception; it does not establish one universal risk hierarchy.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/loth_ai_disinformation_threats_20260729.pdf">Read the research note <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>

    <article class="orientation-card">
      <p class="pathway-number" aria-hidden="true">04</p>
      <p class="orientation-label">Institutional action · August 2026</p>
      <h3>Education and children</h3>
      <p>New U.S. Department of Education guidance asks schools to judge technology by instructional purpose, evidence, transparency, duration, and student outcomes.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://www.ed.gov/about/news/press-release/us-department-of-education-releases-guidance-responsible-use-of-education-technology-classroom">Read the federal guidance <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-shell relationship-intro" aria-labelledby="connections-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The missing view</p>
    <h2 id="connections-heading">The signals are connected.</h2>
    <p>A forecast about jobs changes education choices. AI infrastructure affects energy, water, cost, and climate decisions. Synthetic media changes how people interpret politics and public institutions. Those shifts alter family planning, mental health, trust, investment, and policy in return.</p>
    <p>Hii studies these relationships across systems and over time—not only the stories one by one.</p>
  </div>

